<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Vereya</h1><p class="st-meta">1432 CE – 1486 CE (approx.) · capital Vereya</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last surviving appanage of the Moscow princes, bequeathed to Ivan III after its heir fled to Lithuania.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vereya">Vereya</a>, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, belonged to the lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrey-of-mozhaysk">Andrei of Mozhaysk</a>. In 1432 his younger son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-andreyevich-of-vereya">Mikhail Andreyevich</a> began to rule Vereya together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belozersk">Beloozero</a> as his own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Unlike his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-andreyevich-of-mozhaysk">Ivan of Mozhaysk</a>, Mikhail stayed loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasily-ii-of-moscow">Vasily II</a> during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow's</a> civil war, and he was allowed to keep his lands after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozhaysk">Mozhaysk</a> was taken in 1454. He ruled a small principality of farmland and forest, dependent on the grand prince for protection and politics.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1483 Mikhail's son Vasily, nicknamed the Daring, quarrelled with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> and fled to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>. Mikhail was forced to leave his lands to Ivan III, and on his death in 1486 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vereya">Vereya</a> was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1432 CE – 1486 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="